  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 485,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Chest X-ray (CXR): read it the SAME WAY every time, DRS. ABCDE, so nothing is missed",
   "lines": [
    "Details · RIPE: Rotation (clavicle ends equidistant), Inspiration (anterior ribs 5–6 or posterior 8–10), Picture, Exposure",
    "Soft tissue, bones · Airway, mediastinum: TRACHEA deviated? · Breathing: PNEUMOTHORAX?",
    "Circulation: heart size on a back-to-front (PA) film; a portable front-to-back film magnifies it",
    "Diaphragm: FREE AIR? (see the ACUTE ABDOMEN chart) · Extras: tubes, lines, devices · compare with OLD films"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_w",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 174,
   "w": 900,
   "h": 80,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "WHITE where air should be",
   "lines": [
